  "title": "went, ate, saw — past tense yang berubah bentuk",
  "pattern": "go → went / eat → ate / see → saw / have → had / come → came / buy → bought",
  "explanation": "Justru kata kerja yang paling sering dipakai, past tense-nya tidak memakai -ed tapi berubah bentuk: go → went, eat → ate, see → saw, have → had, come → came, buy → bought. Jumlahnya tidak banyak, jadi hafalkan satu per satu, mulai dari yang paling sering dipakai.",
  "natural": "What did you do yesterday? — I went to the beach. (Apa yang kamu lakukan kemarin? — Saya pergi ke pantai.)",
  "stiff": "goed, eated (menambahkan -ed) itu salah. Setelah did, kata kerjanya kembali ke bentuk dasar: Did you go? (Did you went? salah.)",
